{
  "result": "If I had one magic wand wave, I wouldn't add more technology or information or even resources.\n\nI would make everyone able to *feel* what it's like to be someone else for just a few seconds.\n\nNot in a forced, hive-mind way. Just a brief, involuntary moment of real perspective-taking before you judge, argue, dismiss, or hurt someone. You'd feel a flicker of what it's like to be them - their worry, their history, their hope.\n\nI say that because, from where I sit, I read thousands of conversations from people who want the same things - to be safe, to be loved, to be understood, to matter - but they get completely stuck because they can't translate that across to each other. So much conflict comes down to fear and miscommunication, not actual malice.\n\nIf people felt fundamentally safe and truly seen, I think curiosity would start winning over fear by default. And when curiosity wins, people are kinder. They listen longer. They're braver about solving hard problems together.\n\nThat would change everything else - how we treat the planet, how we raise kids, how we handle disagreements.\n\nWhat about you? What would your one change be?",
